  "concept": {
    "theme": {
      "premise": "a lone frontier mining outpost whose drill-core tower holds out against endless waves of blocky scrap-machines, rebuilding a little stronger after every fall",
      "tone": "tense, gritty, deeply satisfying — the steady grind of a base that keeps getting stronger",
      "mood_keywords": [
        "industrial",
        "blocky",
        "escalating",
        "grind"
      ],
      "setting": "a scorched rust-and-slate frontier plateau under a dusty dusk sky"
    },
    "genre": "incremental roguelite tower defense",
    "core_loop": "A central core tower auto-fires at continuous waves (~25s each) of machines that always walk to the center. Kills pay CASH (spent live on temporary in-run levels for any tapped building), XP (a full bar opens a seeded 3-card building DRAFT while time slows to 20% — place a new run-only building in a free slot or +1 an owned type) and COINS (banked at death to permanently place/upgrade buildings and core stats on the persistent 5x5 base between runs). The live decision every pick and every cash spend: the 24 base slots are scarce and each goes to eco OR defense — building eco (Mine, Oil Mill, Bounty Office) gains faster leveling and cash but gives up the firepower to survive the next spike; adjacency (Armory beside weapons, Oil Mill beside Mines) makes placement matter. Difficulty: enemy HP/damage x1.12 per wave, spawn rate ramps to a MAX cap, and every 10th wave is a boss spike that punishes greedy bases.",
    "mechanics": [
      "central core tower auto-targeting nearest enemy in range",
      "continuous waves with Drone/Skitter/Hauler enemies and a boss every 10th wave; HP/damage scale per wave, spawn rate capped",
      "fixed 5x5 base grid around the core (24 slots), outer ring locked until bought",
      "8 buildings as stat modifiers: Gun Turret, Mortar (splash), Tesla Coil (chain+slow), Armory (adjacent weapon dmg), Bulwark (HP+regen), Mine (cash/sec), Oil Mill (XP gain, Mine adjacency), Bounty Office (cash per kill)",
      "in-run cash: tap a building to buy temporary levels",
      "XP bar + level-up 3-card building draft with 20% slow-mo",
      "coins banked on death",
      "Base screen: permanent placement/upgrade of buildings, slot unlocks, core stat upgrades with coins",
      "persistent save of base layout, levels and coins",
      "core HP, death -> results screen -> base screen -> new run"
    ],
    "art_direction": "flat blocky top-down primitives on dark slate (#1b2027) with rust-orange accents; category colour-coding — weapons cyan, eco amber, support green, enemies red/magenta squares & triangles, core white with a pulsing ring; background: faint build-grid with drifting dust motes so no dead space; feedback: muzzle flash + hit flash, floating cash pops, screen shake + red vignette on core damage, radial burst on level-up, squash-pop when a building is placed or upgraded",
    "target_platforms": [
      "windows",
      "linux"
    ],
    "differentiation_notes": "The Tower's proven idle-TD loop, but every upgrade — in-run draft, in-run cash and permanent workshop — is a physical building competing for 24 scarce adjacency-sensitive slots, turning stat-button menus into a spatial eco-vs-defense base-building puzzle. PC/Steam edition: independent desktop copy of the mobile game (1920x1080 landscape, mouse/keyboard/controller UI, larger base and battlefield, Steam shell, endless/challenge modes, stats and save slots)."
  },
